~ map_dialogue
Alastor : What are those? I have not seen such creatures in my life.
Elliot : Remnants of the ancient war.
Alastor : ?
Alastor : No! That cannot be! You, of all mages, believe in those myths?
Elliot : When you get as old as me, you will be able to believe even the most outrageous claims. Especially when the one saying them is the Archchancellor.
Alastor : …
Elliot : Also, this is a perfect place for them to hide. The place that no fool would be able to leave to tell the tale and no wise men would enter.
Alastor : Heh. Good thing that we are neither. 
Elliot : Hm. Let's wipe them out.
=> END